{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc 'cat /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src/consensus_assurance/resources/skills/consensus-analysis/guide.md /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src/consensus_assurance/resources/skills/consensus-analysis/references/behavior-facts.md; cat ../agent-source/omnipaxos/src/sequence_paxos/leader.rs'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc 'cat /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src/consensus_assurance/resources/skills/consensus-analysis/guide.md /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src/consensus_assurance/resources/skills/consensus-analysis/references/behavior-facts.md; cat ../agent-source/omnipaxos/src/sequence_paxos/leader.rs'","aggregated_output":"# Investigation and selection\n\nCandidate investigates a sourced question, including unknown requirements, protection premises or legal history. Obligation fixes an applicable responsibility without presuming violation; Check supplies inputs, history and observations. Missing authority calls for contract investigation, missing history for source work or conditional exploration. Neither gap bars a Candidate or licenses an invented obligation.\n\nFirst explain both core relationships from activity_roles and their connection in AuditSpec.core_overview. Follow representative work through owners, qualified support, aggregation, decision, propagation and consumption; explain acquisition, change and loss of context/authority and handling of old requests, replies, pending support and established decisions. Read the supporting membership, history, recovery and completion mechanisms needed for this backbone. Trace callers and callees, important rejection, retry and asynchronous paths; deeper variants may remain open.\n\nSave early discrepancies as sourced Surfaces or specific unknowns even when no obligation is ready. Distinguish open_details from core_gaps: unexplained formation, authority transition or old-work handling breaks readiness; a usable overview can retain local anomalies. Only a preconfigured directed_question permits a proportionate local boundary first; activity_focus does not. A usable map and first Candidate may share a product. Unmapped source work and exploration need no fabricated Fact.\n\nUse behavior-facts.md for implementation meaning. Select a principal Fact lifecycle with a sourced A1/A2 connection; a question need not span both. Direct behavior_ids establish, consume, invalidate or reinterpret it; supporting_behavior_ids explain separate history/context/consequence support. Cross-activity effects establish actual relationships without relabeling support Activities. Names and protocol labels establish neither relevance nor responsibility.\n\nUse question, counterevidence, unknowns, importance and trigger_rationale to identify what remains unexplained, what existing protection does establish, and what the next action will distinguish. A concise sourced difference suffices; no ranking, mandatory alternative list or confidence threshold. Compare contract reading, smaller exploration and another known relationship before committing to a costly test. “This input has not been run” alone is not a discriminator. An empty unknowns list does not disqualify a check whose earlier investigation established its value.\n\nWhen sourced mechanisms answer the specific suspicion, submit explained and reselect. An unconstructed single obligation may remain unexecuted; this is neither holds nor a budget refund. Fixed artifacts, directed execution tasks, changed premises and open disputes remain visible until explicitly handled. An explicit guard with unresolved ownership, timing, producer or context instead calls for investigation of that premise. A negative result should identify the plausible explanation it excluded and independent premises left open; distinguish it from execution corroborating an already-explained protection. Neither settles the entire Fact or becomes a reason to expand input variants indefinitely. Keep one requirement's independent scenarios together; a genuinely different responsibility gets its own question.\n\nConditional differences with unclear contracts remain exploration or local pause. Once responsibility is grounded, obligation and construction may be separate products. Reuse helpers and legal prefixes only after checking their entry, caller duties, completion order and fault assumptions for this question. A convenient driver must not exclude permitted overlap that supplied the discriminator, nor assume a looser ordering is legal because it produces a difference. Fixed checks must still exercise the investigated premise; a narrower child cannot settle its parent. Use existing F2/F3 when requirement or scope changes. Finish necessary technical repair and review of accepted work; switching questions preserves its debt.\n\nPrioritize consensus safety and explicitly scoped progress duties. Distinguish a sourced numeric/event deadline, implementation-owned automatic continuation without a numeric deadline, and later work explicitly owed by the caller. No numeric deadline does not preclude investigating lost continuation triggers; the word automatic alone supplies no obligation. A possible later event in a comment is not a guarantee that callers produce it. Independently grounded eligibility, accounting, wakeup or correlation duties can be resolved without a client endpoint or global consequence. Shared facts and helpers transfer understanding, not results.\n\nAt natural handoffs retain the answered proposition and remaining discriminator in feedback using tasks/audit.md references. In the next already-needed related map submission, replace the answered original unknown with its sourced conditional relationship and remove obsolete progress reminders. Correct materially misleading higher-level summaries in that same product before reuse; harmless wording differences need no cleanup turn or whole-map sweep. Preserve independent unknowns and historical inputs. Consult the actual answer and assessment, not an understanding label or reference alone. Use behavior-facts.md for primary ownership instead of copying one answer across layers. Source work and exploration may continue from feedback; near expiry save minimal complete learning.\n\nOpen runs continue investigation until controller time/call or actual interruption boundaries. Empty pending_work or disposed registered questions does not exhaust the frontier: use the overview, other consumers/contexts, Surfaces and unread paths. Unit admission exhaustion still permits sourced Candidates, premise investigation and authorized exploration without immediate escalation. Follow each capacity separately; do not repeat handoffs, rerun explained guards, reuse an old Claim for a new proposition or refill budgets. Take a smaller informative step near expiry. Only a preconfigured finite directed task may complete early. Actual cancellation, safety refusal, permission loss and unrecoverable service/tool failure still stop.\n# Conditions, effects and semantic facts\n\nDescribe sourced owners, triggers, guards, state changes, effects and asynchronous boundaries. For a relevant relationship already read, identify who establishes the fact under which conditions and what its consumer actually requires. Include other read establishment, invalidation or reinterpretation paths; unread paths remain unknown or sourced Surfaces.\n\nShared updates do not imply shared follow-up effects. When one entry establishes a fact and schedules a consumer but another only establishes the fact, preserve that distinction in trigger, important_branches, writes, external_effects or async_boundaries. Do not union effects into an unconditional guarantee. Distinguish possible effects, conditional scheduling and guaranteed completion. A Behavior can cover multiple entries when conditions remain clear; split minimally when owners, completion boundaries or meanings cannot be expressed accurately together. Do not enumerate every branch or duplicate a shared Fact.\n\nFact states the assertion actually established for its identity and validity_context, not the strongest effect seen on any path. Reporting, internal accounting, notification and completed external work are distinct. Trace relevant guard inputs to their producer, update point, owner and completion duty instead of trusting a variable name. Conversely, a missing local field is not a missing guarantee when dispatch, admission, serialization or reset supplies it. Assess the composed producer/consumer protection, not each structure in isolation. Absent direct action is a question: inspect alternative consumers, delayed validation, shared scheduling and recovery for the same object and history before alleging a defect.\n\nUse produces_fact_ids/consumes_fact_ids for established relationships needed by later questions; reverse indexes are derived. No name-based edges, mandatory edges, branch fields or completeness scores. Reference validation proves structure, not equivalent path meaning. Guards and observed differences do not supply normative obligations without applicable sources and reasoning.\n\nUse existing map_changes at natural handoffs. Correcting an overstrong abstraction challenges the specific Candidate premise that depended on it; independent results retain their original basis. Use preserves only when requirements, dependencies and observation scope actually remain applicable. Meaning, identity, context and dependency changes cannot masquerade as clarification. No change means no version; keep history and counterevidence.\n\nKeep one primary home for each kind of knowledge: Behavior owns producer conditions, changes, synchronization, notification and exit mechanisms; Fact owns the assertion for its identity and validity_context; Candidate/feedback owns the question's answer, actual execution and remaining discriminator; Activity/core_overview owns the core connections, higher-level understanding and navigation; Surface owns unread entries and reasons; CheckRun/assessment/review owns experiment progress and judgments. Scope owns exclusions. Preserve substantive overviews without copying the same long answer and residuals through every layer. Mapped means association, not resolution. An explained Candidate needs no challenge merely to restate its protection; changed protection or Fact context does require attribution. Use the guide's natural handoff for answered unknowns and tasks/audit.md for Material and execution references.\nuse super::super::{\n    ballot_leader_election::Ballot,\n    util::{LeaderState, PromiseMetaData},\n};\nuse crate::util::{AcceptedMetaData, WRITE_ERROR_MSG};\n\nuse super::*;\n\nimpl<T, B> SequencePaxos<T, B>\nwhere\n    T: Entry,\n    B: Storage<T>,\n{\n    /// Handle a new leader. Should be called when the leader election has elected a new leader with the ballot `n`\n    /*** Leader ***/\n    pub(crate) fn handle_leader(&mut self, n: Ballot) {\n        if n <= self.leader_state.n_leader || n <= self.internal_storage.get_promise() {\n            return;\n        }\n        #[cfg(feature = \"logging\")]\n        debug!(self.logger, \"Newly elected leader: {:?}\", n);\n        if self.pid == n.pid {\n            self.leader_state =\n                LeaderState::with(n, self.leader_state.max_pid, self.leader_state.quorum);\n            // Flush any pending writes\n            // Don't have to handle flushed entries here because we will sync with followers\n            let _ = self.internal_storage.flush_batch().expect(WRITE_ERROR_MSG);\n            self.internal_storage.set_promise(n).expect(WRITE_ERROR_MSG);\n            /* insert my promise */\n            let na = self.internal_storage.get_accepted_round();\n            let decided_idx = self.get_decided_idx();\n            let accepted_idx = self.internal_storage.get_accepted_idx();\n            let my_promise = Promise {\n                n,\n                n_accepted: na,\n                decided_idx,\n                accepted_idx,\n                log_sync: None,\n            };\n            self.leader_state.set_promise(my_promise, self.pid, true);\n            /* initialise longest chosen sequence and update state */\n            self.state = (Role::Leader, Phase::Prepare);\n            let prep = Prepare {\n                n,\n                decided_idx,\n                n_accepted: na,\n                accepted_idx,\n            };\n            /* send prepare */\n            for pid in &self.peers {\n                self.outgoing.push(Message::SequencePaxos(PaxosMessage {\n                    from: self.pid,\n                    to: *pid,\n                    msg: PaxosMsg::Prepare(prep),\n                }));\n            }\n        } else {\n            self.become_follower();\n        }\n    }\n\n    pub(crate) fn become_follower(&mut self) {\n        self.state.0 = Role::Follower;\n    }\n\n    pub(crate) fn handle_preparereq(&mut self, prepreq: PrepareReq, from: NodeId) {\n        #[cfg(feature = \"logging\")]\n        debug!(self.logger, \"Incoming message PrepareReq from {}\", from);\n        if self.state.0 == Role::Leader && prepreq.n <= self.leader_state.n_leader {\n            self.leader_state.reset_promise(from);\n            self.leader_state.set_latest_accept_meta(from, None);\n            self.send_prepare(from);\n        }\n    }\n\n    pub(crate) fn handle_forwarded_proposal(&mut self, mut entries: Vec<T>) {\n        if !self.accepted_reconfiguration() {\n            match self.state {\n                (Role::Leader, Phase::Prepare) => self.buffered_proposals.append(&mut entries),\n                (Role::Leader, Phase::Accept) => self.accept_entries_leader(entries),\n                _ => self.forward_proposals(entries),\n            }\n        }\n    }\n\n    pub(crate) fn handle_forwarded_stopsign(&mut self, ss: StopSign) {\n        if self.accepted_reconfiguration() {\n            return;\n        }\n        match self.state {\n            (Role::Leader, Phase::Prepare) => self.buffered_stopsign = Some(ss),\n            (Role::Leader, Phase::Accept) => self.accept_stopsign_leader(ss),\n            _ => self.forward_stopsign(ss),\n        }\n    }\n\n    pub(crate) fn send_prepare(&mut self, to: NodeId) {\n        let prep = Prepare {\n            n: self.leader_state.n_leader,\n            decided_idx: self.internal_storage.get_decided_idx(),\n            n_accepted: self.internal_storage.get_accepted_round(),\n            accepted_idx: self.internal_storage.get_accepted_idx(),\n        };\n        self.outgoing.push(Message::SequencePaxos(PaxosMessage {\n            from: self.pid,\n            to,\n            msg: PaxosMsg::Prepare(prep),\n        }));\n    }\n\n    pub(crate) fn accept_entry_leader(&mut self, entry: T) {\n        let accepted_metadata = self\n            .internal_storage\n            .append_entry_with_batching(entry)\n            .expect(WRITE_ERROR_MSG);\n        if let Some(metadata) = accepted_metadata {\n            self.leader_state\n                .set_accepted_idx(self.pid, metadata.accepted_idx);\n            self.send_acceptdecide(metadata);\n        }\n    }\n\n    pub(crate) fn accept_entries_leader(&mut self, entries: Vec<T>) {\n        let accepted_metadata = self\n            .internal_storage\n            .append_entries_with_batching(entries)\n            .expect(WRITE_ERROR_MSG);\n        if let Some(metadata) = accepted_metadata {\n            self.leader_state\n                .set_accepted_idx(self.pid, metadata.accepted_idx);\n            self.send_acceptdecide(metadata);\n        }\n    }\n\n    pub(crate) fn accept_stopsign_leader(&mut self, ss: StopSign) {\n        let accepted_metadata = self\n            .internal_storage\n            .append_stopsign(ss.clone())\n            .expect(WRITE_ERROR_MSG);\n        if let Some(metadata) = accepted_metadata {\n            self.send_acceptdecide(metadata);\n        }\n        let accepted_idx = self.internal_storage.get_accepted_idx();\n        self.leader_state.set_accepted_idx(self.pid, accepted_idx);\n        for pid in self.leader_state.get_promised_followers() {\n            self.send_accept_stopsign(pid, ss.clone(), false);\n        }\n    }\n\n    fn send_accsync(&mut self, to: NodeId) {\n        let current_n = self.leader_state.n_leader;\n        let PromiseMetaData {\n            n_accepted: prev_round_max_promise_n,\n            accepted_idx: prev_round_max_accepted_idx,\n            ..\n        } = &self.leader_state.get_max_promise_meta();\n        let PromiseMetaData {\n            n_accepted: followers_promise_n,\n            accepted_idx: followers_accepted_idx,\n            pid,\n            ..\n        } = self.leader_state.get_promise_meta(to);\n        let followers_decided_idx = self\n            .leader_state\n            .get_decided_idx(*pid)\n            .expect(\"Received PromiseMetaData but not found in ld\");\n        // Follower can have valid accepted entries depending on which leader they were previously following\n        let followers_valid_entries_idx = if *followers_promise_n == current_n {\n            *followers_accepted_idx\n        } else if *followers_promise_n == *prev_round_max_promise_n {\n            *prev_round_max_accepted_idx.min(followers_accepted_idx)\n        } else {\n            followers_decided_idx\n        };\n        let log_sync = self.create_log_sync(followers_valid_entries_idx, followers_decided_idx);\n        self.leader_state.increment_seq_num_session(to);\n        let acc_sync = AcceptSync {\n            n: current_n,\n            seq_num: self.leader_state.next_seq_num(to),\n            decided_idx: self.get_decided_idx(),\n            log_sync,\n            #[cfg(feature = \"unicache\")]\n            unicache: self.internal_storage.get_unicache(),\n        };\n        let msg = Message::SequencePaxos(PaxosMessage {\n            from: self.pid,\n            to,\n            msg: PaxosMsg::AcceptSync(acc_sync),\n        });\n        self.outgoing.push(msg);\n    }\n\n    fn send_acceptdecide(&mut self, accepted: AcceptedMetaData<T>) {\n        let decided_idx = self.internal_storage.get_decided_idx();\n        for pid in self.leader_state.get_promised_followers() {\n            let latest_accdec = self.get_latest_accdec_message(pid);\n            match latest_accdec {\n                // Modify existing AcceptDecide message to follower\n                Some(accdec) => {\n                    accdec.entries.extend(accepted.entries.iter().cloned());\n                    accdec.decided_idx = decided_idx;\n                }\n                // Add new AcceptDecide message to follower\n                None => {\n                    self.leader_state\n                        .set_latest_accept_meta(pid, Some(self.outgoing.len()));\n                    let acc = AcceptDecide {\n                        n: self.leader_state.n_leader,\n                        seq_num: self.leader_state.next_seq_num(pid),\n                        decided_idx,\n                        entries: accepted.entries.clone(),\n                    };\n                    self.outgoing.push(Message::SequencePaxos(PaxosMessage {\n                        from: self.pid,\n                        to: pid,\n                        msg: PaxosMsg::AcceptDecide(acc),\n                    }));\n                }\n            }\n        }\n    }\n\n    fn send_accept_stopsign(&mut self, to: NodeId, ss: StopSign, resend: bool) {\n        let seq_num = match resend {\n            true => self.leader_state.get_seq_num(to),\n            false => self.leader_state.next_seq_num(to),\n        };\n        let acc_ss = PaxosMsg::AcceptStopSign(AcceptStopSign {\n            seq_num,\n            n: self.leader_state.n_leader,\n            ss,\n        });\n        self.outgoing.push(Message::SequencePaxos(PaxosMessage {\n            from: self.pid,\n            to,\n            msg: acc_ss,\n        }));\n    }\n\n    pub(crate) fn send_decide(&mut self, to: NodeId, decided_idx: usize, resend: bool) {\n        let seq_num = match resend {\n            true => self.leader_state.get_seq_num(to),\n            false => self.leader_state.next_seq_num(to),\n        };\n        let d = Decide {\n            n: self.leader_state.n_leader,\n            seq_num,\n            decided_idx,\n        };\n        self.outgoing.push(Message::SequencePaxos(PaxosMessage {\n            from: self.pid,\n            to,\n            msg: PaxosMsg::Decide(d),\n        }));\n    }\n\n    fn handle_majority_promises(&mut self) {\n        let max_promise_sync = self.leader_state.take_max_promise_sync();\n        let decided_idx = self.leader_state.get_max_decided_idx();\n        let mut new_accepted_idx = self\n            .internal_storage\n            .sync_log(self.leader_state.n_leader, decided_idx, max_promise_sync)\n            .expect(WRITE_ERROR_MSG);\n        if !self.accepted_reconfiguration() {\n            if !self.buffered_proposals.is_empty() {\n                let entries = std::mem::take(&mut self.buffered_proposals);\n                new_accepted_idx = self\n                    .internal_storage\n                    .append_entries_without_batching(entries)\n                    .expect(WRITE_ERROR_MSG);\n            }\n            if let Some(ss) = self.buffered_stopsign.take() {\n                self.internal_storage\n                    .append_stopsign(ss)\n                    .expect(WRITE_ERROR_MSG);\n                new_accepted_idx = self.internal_storage.get_accepted_idx();\n            }\n        }\n        self.state = (Role::Leader, Phase::Accept);\n        self.leader_state\n            .set_accepted_idx(self.pid, new_accepted_idx);\n        for pid in self.leader_state.get_promised_followers() {\n            self.send_accsync(pid);\n        }\n    }\n\n    pub(crate) fn handle_promise_prepare(&mut self, prom: Promise<T>, from: NodeId) {\n        #[cfg(feature = \"logging\")]\n        debug!(\n            self.logger,\n            \"Handling promise from {} in Prepare phase\", from\n        );\n        if prom.n == self.leader_state.n_leader {\n            let received_majority = self.leader_state.set_promise(prom, from, true);\n            if received_majority {\n                self.handle_majority_promises();\n            }\n        }\n    }\n\n    pub(crate) fn handle_promise_accept(&mut self, prom: Promise<T>, from: NodeId) {\n        #[cfg(feature = \"logging\")]\n        {\n            let (r, p) = &self.state;\n            debug!(\n                self.logger,\n                \"Self role {:?}, phase {:?}. Incoming message Promise Accept from {}\", r, p, from\n            );\n        }\n        if prom.n == self.leader_state.n_leader {\n            self.leader_state.set_promise(prom, from, false);\n            self.send_accsync(from);\n        }\n    }\n\n    pub(crate) fn handle_accepted(&mut self, accepted: Accepted, from: NodeId) {\n        #[cfg(feature = \"logging\")]\n        trace!(\n            self.logger,\n            \"Got Accepted from {}, idx: {}, chosen_idx: {}, accepted: {:?}\",\n            from,\n            accepted.accepted_idx,\n            self.internal_storage.get_decided_idx(),\n            self.leader_state.accepted_indexes\n        );\n        if accepted.n == self.leader_state.n_leader && self.state == (Role::Leader, Phase::Accept) {\n            self.leader_state\n                .set_accepted_idx(from, accepted.accepted_idx);\n            if accepted.accepted_idx > self.internal_storage.get_decided_idx()\n                && self.leader_state.is_chosen(accepted.accepted_idx)\n            {\n                let decided_idx = accepted.accepted_idx;\n                self.internal_storage\n                    .set_decided_idx(decided_idx)\n                    .expect(WRITE_ERROR_MSG);\n                for pid in self.leader_state.get_promised_followers() {\n                    let latest_accdec = self.get_latest_accdec_message(pid);\n                    match latest_accdec {\n                        Some(accdec) => accdec.decided_idx = decided_idx,\n                        None => self.send_decide(pid, decided_idx, false),\n                    }\n                }\n            }\n        }\n    }\n\n    fn get_latest_accdec_message(&mut self, to: NodeId) -> Option<&mut AcceptDecide<T>> {\n        if let Some((bal, outgoing_idx)) = self.leader_state.get_latest_accept_meta(to) {\n            if bal == self.leader_state.n_leader {\n                if let Message::SequencePaxos(PaxosMessage {\n                    msg: PaxosMsg::AcceptDecide(accdec),\n                    ..\n                }) = self.outgoing.get_mut(outgoing_idx).unwrap()\n                {\n                    return Some(accdec);\n                } else {\n                    #[cfg(feature = \"logging\")]\n                    debug!(self.logger, \"Cached idx is not an AcceptedDecide!\");\n                }\n            }\n        }\n        None\n    }\n\n    pub(crate) fn handle_notaccepted(&mut self, not_acc: NotAccepted, from: NodeId) {\n        if self.state.0 == Role::Leader && self.leader_state.n_leader < not_acc.n {\n            self.leader_state.lost_promise(from);\n        }\n    }\n\n    pub(crate) fn resend_messages_leader(&mut self) {\n        match self.state.1 {\n            Phase::Prepare => {\n                // Resend Prepare\n                let preparable_peers = self.leader_state.get_preparable_peers(&self.peers);\n                for peer in preparable_peers {\n                    self.send_prepare(peer);\n                }\n            }\n            Phase::Accept => {\n                // Resend AcceptStopSign or StopSign's decide\n                if let Some(ss) = self.internal_storage.get_stopsign() {\n                    let decided_idx = self.internal_storage.get_decided_idx();\n                    for follower in self.leader_state.get_promised_followers() {\n                        if self.internal_storage.stopsign_is_decided() {\n                            self.send_decide(follower, decided_idx, true);\n                        } else if self.leader_state.get_accepted_idx(follower)\n                            != self.internal_storage.get_accepted_idx()\n                        {\n                            self.send_accept_stopsign(follower, ss.clone(), true);\n                        }\n                    }\n                }\n                // Resend Prepare\n                let preparable_peers = self.leader_state.get_preparable_peers(&self.peers);\n                for peer in preparable_peers {\n                    self.send_prepare(peer);\n                }\n            }\n            Phase::Recover => (),\n            Phase::None => (),\n        }\n    }\n\n    pub(crate) fn flush_batch_leader(&mut self) {\n        let accepted_metadata = self\n            .internal_storage\n            .flush_batch_and_get_entries()\n            .expect(WRITE_ERROR_MSG);\n        if let Some(metadata) = accepted_metadata {\n            self.leader_state\n                .set_accepted_idx(self.pid, metadata.accepted_idx);\n            self.send_acceptdecide(metadata);\n        }\n    }\n}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"agent_message","text":"I’m applying the supplied consensus-analysis guide. The leader code separates promise collection from acceptance tracking and qualifies both by ballot. I’ll trace the follower guards and recovery paths next to see how old work is handled across authority changes.\n"}}
